Form 49 uses two licenses: one for the code, one for the game content.

1. CODE: MIT License

   Applies to: game.js, style.css, index.html, and the program structure
   of data.js (its variable names, object layout and logic). The general
   techniques in game.js (drawing helpers, particles, animation, rules
   engine) are MIT, but the specific characters and scenes it draws are
   content (see section 2).

2. GAME CONTENT: All rights reserved

   Applies to: all written content (every name, line of dialogue, deed,
   memo, rule text, joke, character and story element, including the text
   strings in data.js), the game title "Form 49", and all artwork, pixel
   art, sound and music, whether drawn in code or stored as files.

   Copyright (c) 2026 karnophage. All rights reserved. You may not copy,
   modify, distribute, or sell this content, or any game built on it,
   without written permission.

If you are unsure which part something falls under, treat it as content.

